{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-1","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-326","text":"WRLM"}]},{"id":"blk-2","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-327","text":"WRLM is an "},{"id":"spn-328","marks":["bold"],"text":"admitted generative transducer"},{"id":"spn-329","text":": a probabilistic proposer over "},{"id":"spn-330","text":"deterministic sealed worlds. It is the "},{"id":"spn-331","marks":["bold"],"text":"only statistical component"},{"id":"spn-332","text":" in the TRVM stack — every other layer is total, deterministic, content-addressed, "},{"id":"spn-333","text":"non-statistical."}]},{"id":"blk-3","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-334","text":"Architecture: Arm D′"}]},{"id":"blk-4","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-335","text":"The model emits full WRL text; the host parses it into an isolated candidate buffer, "},{"id":"spn-336","text":"runs "},{"id":"spn-337","marks":["code"],"text":"diagnose_core"},{"id":"spn-338","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-339","marks":["code"],"text":"seal"},{"id":"spn-340","text":", derives a typed "},{"id":"spn-341","marks":["code"],"text":"GraphEditV1"},{"id":"spn-342","text":" op sequence via "},{"id":"spn-343","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic_diff"},{"id":"spn-344","text":", and applies it through the existing edit algebra. The ops are "},{"id":"spn-345","marks":["bold"],"text":"derived, not generated"},{"id":"spn-346","text":" — capturing the model's accuracy (prose is its strongest modality), the edit algebra's "},{"id":"spn-347","text":"safety (nothing reaches the world except through six typed ops), and typed supervision for RLVR."}]},{"id":"blk-5","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-348","text":"The oracle ladder"}]},{"id":"blk-6","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-8","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-349","text":"Validity — does it parse, seal, and lower? (total, free)"}]}],"id":"blk-7","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-10","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-350","text":"Target identity — is it the intended world? (total, free; sem- equality)"}]}],"id":"blk-9","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-12","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-351","text":"Goal satisfaction — does it meet a stated property? (total, free; GoalSpecV1)"}]}],"id":"blk-11","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-352","text":"Subjective quality — not available; out of scope for WRLM-0"}]}],"id":"blk-13","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-15","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-353","text":"Acceptance policy"}]},{"id":"blk-16","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-354","text":"Admission is governed by the existing "},{"id":"spn-355","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"bend:d3vixl0"}],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-356","text":" kernel — no new policy language. Gate order: "},{"id":"spn-357","marks":["bold"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ resource-compliant ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-358","text":"."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-18","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-359","text":"Build-order steps 1–2 shipped and closed: GoalSpecV1, TaskBundleV1, WorldRecordV1, the coverage domain (320 cells), a 58-world proved pool. Steps 3–10 remain paper only."}]}],"id":"blk-17","kind":"quote"}],"edges":[{"object":"bend:d377lmi","predicate":"ampersand.docs:proposes-to","subject":"bend:dykurqf"},{"object":"bend:d3vixl0","predicate":"ampersand.docs:governed-by","subject":"bend:dykurqf"},{"object":"bend:d1fpdh60","predicate":"ampersand.docs:admitted-by","subject":"bend:dykurqf"},{"object":"bend:d4hgjw0","predicate":"ampersand.docs:measured-by","subject":"bend:dykurqf"}],"id":"bagaaierafp2m7wim43suu3kvptonnd2baed4ijesfgsrdzfizgwnvnh3hh3q","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.v1"}